## ARTIFACT TYPES

### A) Core Runtime Artifacts

| Type | File Pattern | What It Contains |
|------|-------------|------------------|
| **FLOW** | `flow.xml` | Flow Service implementation — executable logic and control flow (MAP, INVOKE, BRANCH, SEQUENCE, LOOP, EXIT, REPEAT, TRY/CATCH) |
| **NDF** | `node.ndf` | Service/docType/schema/adapter/web-service metadata — signatures, properties, references |
| **IDF** | `node.idf` | Namespace/package/folder descriptor metadata — hierarchy and organization |

### B) Security & Contract Artifacts

| Type | File Pattern | What It Contains |
|------|-------------|------------------|
| **ACL** | `*_nodesACL.xml` | Access control definitions — execute/read/write/list permissions per service node |
| **WSDL** | `.wsdl`, `.wsd`, extensionless `wsdl0` | SOAP contract definitions — operations, messages, types, bindings |
| **XSD** | `.xsd` | XML schema artifacts — types, constraints, structures |
| **DOC** | NDF-based docType structures | Document type representations used by flows and mappings |

### C) Code & Supporting Artifacts

| Type | File Pattern | What It Contains |
|------|-------------|------------------|
| **JAVA** | `.java`, `java.frag` | Java Service code — pipeline manipulation, custom logic, external library integration (`.java` = source; `java.frag` = base64-encoded fragment) |
| **TRIGGER** | `node.ndf` in `ns/.../triggers/` | Pub/sub trigger definitions — subscription filters, called services, messaging configuration |
| **Config** | `.xml`, `.json`, `.properties`, `.yaml/.yml`, `.cnf`, `.frg`, `apigateway.cnf` | Runtime-relevant descriptors, package config, API Gateway exposure config, metadata exports |
| **API Gateway** | `.acdl`, `ExportReport.json`, policy/action files | API exposure, policy intent, alias definitions |

**Rule:** If an artifact type is absent in a given project, explicitly state: *"Not present in provided artifacts."*

